/obj/item/paper{
	desc = info;
	info = "SITE-104 RESEARCH DEPARTMENT FORM 9-F<br><br><b><i>NON-HAZARDOUS ANOMALOUS FAUNA LISTING</i></b><br><b>Issuing Department:</b> Research Department - Xenobiological Intake Desk<br><b>Revision:</b> 9-F-RD-FAUNA<br><b>Clearance Requirement:</b> <i>Level 1 or higher (Public Posting Copy)</i><br><b>Handling Category:</b> Ongoing Registration of Non-Hazardous Anomalous Organism<br><br><b>SECTION A - REGISTERING PERSONNEL INFORMATION</b><br>A-1. Full Name: <i>Dr. R. Okonkwo-Vance</i><br>A-2. Assigned Division/Department: <i>Research - Veterinary Liaison</i><br>A-3. Current Clearance Level: <i>2 (Verified)</i><br>A-4. Supervisor (if applicable): <i>Site Command, courtesy notice only</i><br><br><b>SECTION B - ENTITY IDENTIFICATION</b><br>B-1. Entity Designation: <i>"Batsy" (informal); no numerical designation assigned</i><br>B-2. Entity Classification Category:<br> (Select all that Apply)[X] <i>Non-Hazardous</i>- [ ] <i>Thaumiel</i>- [ ] <i>Restricted</i>- [ ] <i>Hazard-Adjacent</i>- [X] <i>Sensitive</i><br>B-3. Current Location: <i>At large, rig-wide — most frequently Mining Deck exterior catwalks, lowest level</i><br>B-4. Physical Condition on Intake:<br><i>Domestic short-hair cat, adult, good health. Genetic screening flagged non-terrestrial sequences spliced with standard feline DNA. Found in a mislabeled supply crate ("MISC.LABSUNDRIES") during routine transfer; no manifest entry accounted for her.</i><br>(Attach additional sheets if necessary.)<br><br><b>SECTION C - PURPOSE OF REGISTRATION</b><br>C-1. Authorized Research Activity / Test Designation: <i>None — observational only</i><br>C-2. Summary of Intended Use (<i>mandatory</i>):<br><i>Entity is not to be subject to testing or removal. This form exists to formally log her presence, movement pattern, and the below cross-department advisory, so future staff do not mistake her for a containment breach.</i><br><br>[<i>To be reviewed by the vault officer</i>]<br><b>SECTION D - USAGE LIMITATIONS</b><br>By signing below, the requester acknowledges the following mandatory restrictions:<br>- Entity MUST NOT be relocated, contained, or removed from the rig.<br>- Entity MUST be left undisturbed if found resting on exterior catwalk railings or gratings.<br>- Testing may be permitted with advanced notice.<br>- Required Return Time:<br>-[ ] <i>2 hours</i>- [ ] <i>4 hours</i>- [ ] <i>End of Shift</i>- [X] <i>Other:</i> <i>N/A — permanent resident</i><br><br><b>SECTION E - SIGNATURES</b><br>Requester Signature: <i>R. Okonkwo-Vance</i> Date: <i>______/______/______</i><br>Supervising Researcher (if required): <i>N/A</i><br><br>Research Officer Authorizing Registration:<br>Name: <i>Site Command (Delegated)</i> Signature: <i>[illegible]</i><br><br>Entity Logged By (Intake Desk): <i>R. Okonkwo-Vance</i><br><br><b>FOR RESEARCH USE ONLY</b><br><i>Cross-Department Notes:</i> <i>Thaumaturgy Dept. flags repeatable low-level thaumic resonance along Batsy's preferred catwalk routes, pattern loosely consistent with minor ward-craft signatures. Origin unconfirmed — possible residual effect of splicing process. Thaumaturgy's formal request to "consult" with subject near active ritual work has been denied twice by Site Command.</i><br><i>Status:</i> [X] Cleared for Continued Free Roam. [ ] Sent for Decon. [ ] Hold for Review<br><i>Chain-of-Custody Verified By: (If Applicable)</i> <i>N/A</i><br>";
	name = "Research Form 9-F: Batsy The Cat"
	},
